  "description": "Overview Hackignite 1.0 is a national-level 24-hour hackathon organised by Computer Science and Engineering (CSE/AIML) at Jain College of Engineering and Technology, Hubballi, on 12th and 13th of December 2026. Eligibility Criteria Open to undergraduate students from recognized colleges across India. Each team must consist of 3–4 members. Every participant must carry a valid college ID card. Registration Fees: Rs 2000 per team Have any queries : https://hk-seven-psi.vercel.app/ Domains: Web development App development Important Dates: 28/11/2026 Last date for registration. 12/12/2026 Hackathon begins. 13/12/2026 Hackathon ends. Event Highlights: 24 Hours of Non-Stop Innovation Exciting Cash Prize (Prize Pool upto Rs 40,000 ) Hands-on Coding and Development Industry-Oriented Problem Solving Project Demonstrations and Evaluation Physical Certificates for All Participants Rules and Regulations: All participants must complete registration before the deadline. Each team must have a minimum of 3 and a maximum of 4 members. Team members cannot be changed after registration. Participants must carry their valid college ID cards. All project development must take place during the hackathon period. Pre-built projects will not be accepted as original hackathon submissions. Use of AI tools is permitted. Plagiarism or copying other teams projects may lead to disqualification. Teams must present their working prototype during the final evaluation. The judges decision will be final.",
